  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="13.3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIIAtr">III Atr</ref> 13.3</head>
        <ab type="selectedText" xml:lang="und">⁊ þar þegen áge twegen costas, lufe oððe lage, ⁊ he þonne lufe geceose, stande þæt swa fæst swa sé dom.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en">And where a thegn has two alternatives before him—amicable agreement or legal proceedings—and he decides upon the former, it shall be as binding as a legal decision.</ab>
        <ab type="supplementaryText" xml:lang="und">Et ubi tainus habet duas optiones. amicitie uel lage, et amicitiam eliget, stet hoc ita firmum sicut ipsum iudicium.</ab>
      </div>
    </body>
